 [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "28 July 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2167"} "Grand Palais, Paris, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2011470"} "34 from 18 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/126517"} "Lee Kiefer"] " of the United States was the defending gold medalist and was world ranked #1 coming into Paris. She was expected to be challenged by a group of Italians who held the 2-5 world ranking positions – " [:a {:href "/athletes/2505325"} "Martina Favaretto"] " (2), " [:a {:href "/athletes/144048"} "Alice Volpi"] " (3), " [:a {:href "/athletes/123944"} "Arianna Errigo"] " (4), and " [:a {:href "/athletes/144050"} "Martina Batini"] " (5). The seedings did not quite follow the rankings as Errigo was seeded #1 in Paris. Only three Italians could be entered in the event and Batini was left out."] "\n\n" [:p {} "All four favorites made the quarter-finals, where Errigo was upset by American " [:a {:href "/athletes/151977"} "Lauren Scruggs"] " and Favaretto lost out to Canadian " [:a {:href "/athletes/129452"} "Eleanor Harvey"] ", although Volpi and Kiefer advanced to meet each other in the semi-final. Kiefer defeated Volpi easily, 15-10, while Scruggs set up an all-American final by defeating Harvey, 15-9."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Kiefer defended her gold medal, having an easy time with her teammate, winning 15-6. This was only the fourth time one nation had gone 1-2 in women’s individual foil, and the first since 2012, when " [:a {:href "/athletes/123942"} "Elisa Di Francisca"] " won gold with Errigo taking silver."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the bronze medal match, Eleanor Harvey prevailed, upsetting Volpi, 15-12, making it an all-North American podium. Italy had no medals, but Volpi, Errigo, and Favaretto finished 4-5-6, in that order."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Kiefer became only the third fencer to defend Olympic gold in women’s individual foil, after Hungary’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/20737"} "Ilona Elek-Schacherer"] " in 1936-48, and Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/20803"} "Valentina Vezzali"] ", who won three consecutive golds from 2000-08."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Seed"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/126517"} "Lee Kiefer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "9"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/151977"} "Lauren Scruggs"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "12"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/129452"} "Eleanor Harvey"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/144048"} "Alice Volpi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/123944"} "Arianna Errigo"]] [:td {} [: